edits.sketch:
New action, registered as "feature_stage_route" (edit 2). Config: plan_field, state_field, branch_prefix=feat/ (D2), require_fresh_branch=true (E4), repo_owner/repo_name. On first invocation it derives branch feat/<short> and, if require_fresh_branch, refuses a pre-existing branch via a READ-ONLY existence check:
    if datahelpers.GetBoolField(config, "require_fresh_branch", true) {
        exists, err := githubBranchExists(ctx, owner, repo, branch)   // GET api.github.com/.../branches/<b>, writes nothing
        ...
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("branch %s already exists — delete the stale branch before re-firing (E4)", branch)
    }
Branch CREATION is NOT here — it stays on the git-adapter create_branch verb before the loop. Each iteration emits stage_plan (the stage's edits[] as a single-plan), read_ref (base for stage 1, the feat branch after), the per-stage commit message/gate flags, and has_more; the terminal emits the PR payload (post_merge_checklist as an owner task list) and the go-test packages DERIVED from the plan's .go edits (D6). A mid-run unreadable feature_state is a hard error ('refusing to re-seed mid-run', line 142) — never a silent restart from stage 1 onto a branch that already has commits.

